id: frosted
name: Frosted
kind: conditions
# One stack per clock, so the Square stays Frozen until the last attacker's clock runs out
# rather than the first. The cap only has to be out of anybody's reach, as Ignited's does.
maxStacks: 99
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry makes a Square Frozen and never names one.
combatCondition: no
# The Environmental Quality this mark puts on the Square while it is held. Named here and
# not in the code, where no Quality is named.
quality: frozen
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The ground under you has frozen over. Your Square is Frozen.
text: >
  Frosted: the Elemental (Ice) Profile's mark. "Any Squares occupied by Character(s) who
  take Damage from this Attacking Maneuver become Frozen (see — Environmental Qualities,
  Battle Environments) until the start of your next turn."

---

# --- The name is this system's ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Ignited's twin: the entry makes a Square Frozen, this system has no Squares, and the
# Environmental Qualities are on the character. So the ice lands on whoever took the
# Damage, as a mark on the attacker's clock, and `qualitiesOf` adds the Quality in the
# `quality:` header while it is held. The player's own ticks are never written to.
#
# No effects of its own. What frozen ground does is the Frozen Quality's file - its Ki
# Point loss at either end of the turn. Its Movement rider is not built there either:
# there is no Movement here for it to slow.
